HOW THIS REORDERS THE Ir RANKING (`compute_stats_x86_recheck_2026-09-05`
§4a, same cell, same commit):

  * **`cost_coeffs_txb` flips from a loss to the port's biggest win.** The Ir
    ranking put it at #10 with a 18.8 M-Ir excess (1.18x). By cycles it is
    0.71x C — the port runs 1.07x C's instructions there at IPC 5.02 against
    C's 3.34, and SAVES 2.35 % of its own frame against C. Do not "fix" it.
  * **The allocator/zero-fill family moves to #1.** The Ir ranking listed
    memset at #2 with the standing warning that its bytes are double-counted
    with the allocator edge; by cycles the whole family (memset + memmove +
    calloc + free + malloc, port-and-C alike) is the largest single excess at
    +5.84 % of the port's frame. The overlap warning still holds and is
    CONFIRMED here: 54,437,292 of the port's 78,128,871 memset Ir (70 %) come
    from one unnamed frame under the allocator, i.e. the `vec![0; n]`
    zero-fill behind `__rust_alloc_zeroed`, not from a caller-visible
    `fill(0)`. The named callers in the port's tree are all small
    (`build_coeff_cost_tables_from_fc` 11,050 Ir,
    `wiener_convolve_add_src::{closure#1}` 5,328, `predict_unit_overlay`
    3,550). The sites are the ones `callcount_realimg_2026-09-04` §B already
    named — `tx_pipeline.rs:619` (`vec![0i32; pw*ph]`), `tx_pipeline.rs:718`
    (`vec![0u8; n]`), `predict.rs:153-154`.
  * **CDEF drops from #1 to #2** but stays large and gets a mechanism: C's
    `svt_cdef_filter_block_8xn_8_avx2` runs at IPC 5.30 while the port's
    `cdef_filter_block_core` runs at 3.01, so the port loses on BOTH counts.
  * **`MD quantize kernels` and `inverse transform` join `cost_coeffs_txb`
    below zero** — the port is cheaper than C in cycles at all three.
  * `Wiener compute_stats` stays at the bottom, 1.19x by cycles, exactly as
    the recheck said. `Wiener convolve` stays large (53.65x by cycles against
    the recheck's 52.78x by Ir).

TWO ROWS ARE NOT USABLE AS RATIOS, for the reason the recheck record already
gave: `PD0 quantize core` compares the port's `pd0::tx_quant_core` (which
keeps the work in itself) against C's `svt_aom_quantize_inv_quantize_light`
(which keeps almost nothing in self and calls out), and `residual` /
`LR other (search/apply/sse)` / `CDEF search driver` have port-only or
inlined-away counterparts. The TSV flags each with
"SELF-vs-INCLUSIVE artifact" or "NO C SYMBOL MATCHED".

Content check: the same table for screen_terminal p6 keeps the allocator at
#1 (+7.15 %) and Wiener convolve at #2 (+5.89 %); photo_cid p2 keeps the
allocator at #1 (+4.93 %) with forward transform (+3.66 %) and RDOQ
(+2.88 %) next, and `cost_coeffs_txb` is a win on all three cells
(-2.35 / -2.47 / -0.86 %).

A THING THE Ir CAMPAIGN COULD NOT SEE, AND SHOULD RECORD: **valgrind masks
AVX-512, so every callgrind number for C is C's AVX2 arm — but on this host
C RUNS AVX-512.** The hardware profile shows C executing
`svt_spatial_full_distortion_kernel_avx512`, `svt_av1_fwd_txfm2d_16x16_avx512`,
`fdct16x16_avx512`, `fdct32x32_avx512`, `av1_fdct64_new_avx512`,
`transpose_16nx16n_avx512`, `svt_av1_txb_init_levels_avx512`,
`compute_stats_win5_avx512.constprop.0` and
`svt_av1_wiener_convolve_add_src_avx512`. The port executes NO AVX-512
kernel of its own — its only avx512 symbols are libc's memset/memmove. The
net effect on totals is small (C's hardware instruction count is 5.4 % below
its callgrind Ir at p6, the port's 4.8 % below), so the Ir ranking is not
badly distorted overall; per kernel it can be, and an AVX-512 archmage tier
is unmeasured headroom that no Ir number in this campaign can price.

The archmage dispatch boundary is NOT a stall site: the `__arcane_*_impl_v3`
kernels run at IPC 3.13-4.97 (nz_map 4.79, cdef_filter_block 4.97,
compute_stats 4.95, sse 4.20, quantize_fp 4.23), at or above the port's frame
average. The out-of-line dispatchers cost 0.67 % of the p6 frame in total
(`fwd_txfm2d_dispatch` 0.26 %, `inv_txfm2d_dispatch_bd` 0.21 %,
`inv_txfm2d_dispatch` 0.20 %) at IPC 2.2-2.8 — a real but small tax, and not
a stall.

=================== 5. QUESTION 3 — WHERE SAFE RUST COSTS INSTRUCTIONS ===================

Not guessed: `objdump -d` of the release binary with GOT-indirect call
targets resolved through `.rela.dyn` `R_X86_64_RELATIVE` (this matters — a
first pass that read only the direct `call <symbol>` form found ZERO
`panic_bounds_check` sites and was WRONG; the panic calls go through the
GOT, e.g. `call *0x240045(%rip)  # 30c380` where slot 0x30c380 relocates to
0x2ed75f = `core::panicking::panic_bounds_check`).

Whole binary, 574,540 instructions of `.text` (2,279,374 bytes), 17,668 call
sites: **2,042 `panic_bounds_check`, 721 slice-index-fail, 171
`unwrap_failed`, 939 other panic, 665 `memcpy`/`memmove`, 290 `memset`,
3,964 allocator.**

Where they sit in the hot code (SAFETY_FN rows), bounds / slice-index sites
per function:

  function                                             insns  bounds  sliceidx
  quant::optimize_b::{closure#0}                        4,721     72        0
  dsp::inv_txfm::idct64                                 8,157     69        0
  dsp::fwd_txfm::fdct64                                 4,361     66        0
  dsp::inv_txfm::idct32                                 2,866     36        0
  dsp::fwd_txfm::fdct32                                 1,645     34        0
  leaf_funnel::tx_pipeline::tx_unit_inner               2,268     13       18
  entropy::coeff_simd::__arcane_nz_map_ctxs_impl_v3       832      5       26
  leaf_funnel::coeff_rate::cost_coeffs_txb_inner::{c#0}   274     15        0
  dsp::cdef::cdef_filter_block_core                       458      8        0
  pd0::tx_quant_core                                    1,139      5        2
  entropy::coeff_c::write_coeffs_txb_1d                 1,956      1        0
  leaf_funnel::coeff_rate::cost_coeffs_txb                761      1        1
  dsp::restoration::__arcane_compute_stats_impl_v3      7,553      2        2

**`optimize_b::{closure#0}` is the port's largest single cycle consumer
(16.35 % of the p6 frame, 27.96 % of the p2 frame) AND carries 72 retained
bounds checks in 4,721 instructions — one every 66.** `cost_coeffs_txb_inner`
carries 15 in 274 instructions — one every 18. The 64- and 32-point
transform butterflies (`fdct64` 66, `idct64` 69, `fdct32` 34, `idct32` 36)
are the classic case the workspace's own guidance names: they index long
slices with runtime offsets where a single
`try_into::<&[T; N]>()` at the function boundary would let LLVM prove the
whole body in range. `nz_map_ctxs` and `tx_unit_inner` are dominated by the
slice-RANGE form (26 and 18 sites), i.e. `&buf[a..b]` sub-slicing rather than
scalar indexing.

The instruction cost these carry is NOT isolated in this record — a bounds
check is a `cmp`+`jae` pair on the fast path and callgrind attributes both to
the source line of the indexing expression, so they cannot be separated from
the loop's own arithmetic. What IS measured is the aggregate signature they
produce: the port executes one branch every 6.1 instructions against C's one
every 9.1-10.9, and 3.0-4.1x C's absolute branch count.

The generic-library cost is measurable directly, because callgrind
attributes inlined `core` code to the `core` source line. Port SELF Ir at
photo_cid p6, by `core` source line:

  RUSTLIB line                          what it is                Ir      % frame   Bc          Bcm
  core/src/cmp.rs:1077                  `Ord::min` body      58,232,495   3.60 %   6,873,220   226,285
  core/src/cmp.rs:1916                  PartialOrd lt/le     45,279,175   2.80 %      23,974     1,401
  core/src/num/uint_macros.rs:1052      `checked_sub`        43,470,799   2.68 %  20,163,218   280,278
  core/src/iter/range.rs:900            `Range::spec_next`   41,203,343   2.54 %  21,531,975 1,987,171
  core/src/num/int_macros.rs:2486       `wrapping_abs`       25,004,998   1.54 %           0         0
  core/src/num/uint_macros.rs:973       `unchecked_add` path 18,792,813   1.16 %           0         0
  core/src/num/int_macros.rs:3634       `i32::abs`           16,227,083   1.00 %           0         0
  core/src/cmp.rs:2025                  `clamp`              14,519,773   0.90 %   2,786,962    19,790
  core/src/ops/range.rs:563             `Range::is_empty`     9,247,775   0.57 %   6,184,882    40,035
  (plus core/src/cmp.rs and core/src/num/uint_macros.rs line-0 rollups,
   core/src/iter/range.rs rollup, core/src/slice/iter/macros.rs:180 5.8 M,
   core/src/iter/adapters/zip.rs:300 7.1 M)

**Those nine lines are 271,978,254 Ir; with the file rollups listed under
them the total is 317,696,743 Ir — 19.6 % of the port's p6 frame —
attributed to `core` library source rather than to the port's own lines.** Two honest
qualifications. (a) C performs the same min/max/abs/clamp/loop-control work;
it is simply attributed to C's own lines because there is no separate
library source to blame. This number is therefore a LOCALISATION, not an
overhead. (b) `Ord::min` at 3.60 % of the frame compiles to a BRANCH
(6,873,220 conditional branches on that one line), not to a `cmov` or a
`pminsd` — that part IS an abstraction cost, and it is the largest single
one. `checked_sub` at 2.68 % is the `Option`-returning form the brief asked
about: 20,163,218 conditional branches on the `if self < rhs` test.

`Range::spec_next` (`for i in 0..n`) is 2.54 % of the frame and 21.5 M
branches. The simulator charges it 21.5 % of the port's frame mispredicts,
but that is the toy predictor failing on loop exits — the hardware says the
port mispredicts LESS than C overall, so do NOT read this line as a
misprediction problem. It is a loop-control INSTRUCTION cost.

Two scalar loops in kernels that C runs as SIMD, both found at the source
line by the same method:
  * `svtav1-dsp/src/restoration.rs:215-221` — the Wiener 7-tap trial filter's
    inner accumulate, `sum += i32::from(rows[k][x]) * i32::from(fk)`, is a
    scalar double loop (line 219 alone is 12,068,864 Ir). C runs
    `svt_av1_wiener_convolve_add_src_avx512`. This is the mechanism behind
    the 53.65x on the ranking's row 5.
  * `svtav1-dsp/src/variance.rs:212-219` — `sse`'s scalar
    `diff = src[..] - ref_[..]; sse += diff*diff` carries 21,363,780 Ir of
    `__arcane_sse_impl_v3`'s 27,915,788 self Ir, i.e. most of the "SIMD"
    kernel's cost is on a scalar line. C runs
    `svt_spatial_full_distortion_kernel_avx512`.

The ONE genuine stall item, and its file:line: **`pipeline.rs::encode_block_syntax`
is the only pair in the ranking where the port's IPC is materially worse
than C's — 1.76 against 3.33** (per-function: port 1.50 against the port's
own 3.44 frame average). It is 2.82 % of the p6 frame cycles for 1.22 % of
the instructions, takes 8.07 % of the port's branch misses and 2.86 % of its
L1D misses, and 82 % of its mispredicts land on the single line
`pipeline.rs:9333` described in §3. Running it at the port's own average IPC
would save 713,938,665 of its 1,261,003,911 cycles — 1.60 % of the frame.
Note the content dependence: at screen_terminal p6 the same function runs at
IPC 3.43, i.e. at the frame average, so this is a photo-content finding.

=================== 6. WHAT TO FIX NEXT, BY MEASURED COST ===================

Category key: [I] instruction count, [C] cache, [B] branch, [S] safe-Rust
construct. Every item below is [I] or [S] except one — that is the finding.

  1. [S] Allocator + zero-fill traffic. +5.84 % of the p6 frame (+7.15 %
     screenshot, +4.93 % p2), 8.23x C's cycles. 70 % of the memset bytes are
     the `vec![0; n]` zero-fill under `__rust_alloc_zeroed`. Sites already
     named: `leaf_funnel/tx_pipeline.rs:619`, `:718`,
     `leaf_funnel/predict.rs:153-154`. Fix shape: the thread-local scratch
     the repo already has (`TX_SCRATCH`, `SatdScratch`), extended to these.
     Not a cache problem — the misses it generates are write-allocate on
     fresh pages and never reach DRAM (port LL misses 128,472 vs C's
     132,781).
  2. [I] CDEF filter kernels. +5.74 %, 10.39x cycles, 7.08x instructions,
     port IPC 3.43 vs C 5.03 (C's `svt_cdef_filter_block_8xn_8_avx2` reaches
     5.30). `svtav1-dsp/src/cdef.rs:cdef_filter_block_core` — 458
     instructions, 8 retained bounds checks, and `Ord::min` inlined into it
     for 11,044,630 Ir.
  3. [I] Entropy coefficient writer. +5.05 %, 3.42x cycles, 4.28x
     instructions, 13.27 % of the port's branch misses.
     `entropy/coeff_c.rs:write_coeffs_txb_1d` (+ `entropy/cdf.rs:74-80`, the
     CDF update, 9,688,320 Ir on line 78 alone).
  4. [I] Range coder. +3.80 %, 3.34x cycles. `entropy/range_coder.rs`
     `normalize` (IPC 2.50) + `encode_cdf_q15`; line 98's
     `if s > 0 { icdf[s-1] } else { 32768 }` mispredicts at 27.33 %.
  5. [S] Wiener trial filter. +3.16 %, 53.65x cycles.
     `svtav1-dsp/src/restoration.rs:215-221` is scalar; C runs an AVX-512
     convolve. This is the item the compute_stats recheck named as what is
     left inside loop restoration, now priced in cycles.
  6. [I] Forward transform. +2.61 %, 1.75x cycles. The port has no AVX-512
     tier; C runs `fdct16x16_avx512` / `fdct32x32_avx512` /
     `av1_fdct64_new_avx512` / `transpose_16nx16n_avx512` here. `fdct64`
     carries 66 retained bounds checks in 4,361 instructions and `fdct32` 34
     in 1,645 — the fixed-size-array boundary pattern applies.
  7. [B] Block syntax packing. +2.36 %, and the ONLY item whose cost is
     stall rather than volume: IPC 1.76 vs C's 3.33, 1.60 % of the frame
     recoverable at the port's own average IPC. Fix: replace the forward
     full-block eob scans at `pipeline.rs:9332-9336` and
     `pipeline.rs:9410-9415` with the reverse-scan-and-return already
     written at `quant.rs:318-324`. Evidence: 316,928 simulated mispredicts
     at 17.16 % on `pipeline.rs:9333` against 89,502 at 3.10 % on
     `quant.rs:320`.
  8. [S] `Ord::min` compiled as a branch — 58,232,495 Ir (3.60 % of the p6
     frame) and 6,873,220 conditional branches on `core/src/cmp.rs:1077`,
     with `cmp.rs:2025` (`clamp`) another 0.90 %. Largest callers are
     `optimize_b` (48,294,231 Ir of `core/src/cmp.rs` inlined) and
     `cdef_filter_block_core` (11,044,630). Worth an experiment with a
     branchless form in those two bodies; not a blanket change.
  9. [S] Retained bounds checks in the two biggest consumers:
     `quant::optimize_b::{closure#0}` (72 sites / 4,721 instructions;
     16.35 % of the p6 frame and 27.96 % of the p2 frame) and
     `coeff_rate::cost_coeffs_txb_inner::{closure#0}` (15 / 274). The
     fixed-size-array boundary (`try_into::<&[T; N]>()` once) is the
     documented pattern. NOTE the ordering caution: `cost_coeffs_txb` as a
     whole is already 0.71x C's cycles, so this is about widening a win, not
     closing a loss.
 10. [I] The out-of-line dispatchers, 0.67 % of the p6 frame at IPC 2.2-2.8
     (`fwd_txfm2d_dispatch` 0.26 %, `inv_txfm2d_dispatch_bd` 0.21 %,
     `inv_txfm2d_dispatch` 0.20 %). Small, real, and NOT a stall.

DO NOT "FIX": `coeff_rate::cost_coeffs_txb` (0.71x C by cycles),
`MD quantize kernels` (0.58x), `inverse transform` (0.88x), `Wiener
compute_stats` (1.19x, already closed by the C-shape rewrite). Three of
these read as port LOSSES in the Ir ranking.

=================== WHAT IS AND IS NOT ESTABLISHED ===================

ESTABLISHED, on three byte-identical cells at this commit on this host:
the hardware instruction / cycle / IPC table and every derived rate in it;
the deterministic cache and branch simulation totals and their per-1000-Ir
rates; the per-function cycles/instructions/IPC/branch-miss/L1D-miss
attribution for both sides; the reordered port-vs-C ranking by cycles; the
static bounds-check / memcpy / allocator census with GOT resolution; the
file:line of the port's largest mispredict site and of the two scalar
kernels named in §5.

NOT MEASURED HERE, and not to be inferred: the Zen 4 mispredict PENALTY in
cycles (so no "branch misses cost N % of the frame" number appears above —
only counts and rates); the split of the port's excess branch instructions
between bounds checks and loop control (they cannot be separated by source
line); any A/B of a proposed fix (this is a measure-only chunk — nothing was
changed); aarch64; 10-bit; inter frames; presets other than 2 and 6; qp
other than 40; the CLIC photo, the line-art and the 500x332 cells;
wall-clock paired timing (cycles on a pinned core are the proxy used; the
harness's own single-run ENCODE_NS agrees with the cycle ratio to 0.4 % at
p6 and 2.9 % at p2, which is single-run scatter, not a second measurement); whether an
AVX-512 archmage tier would recover the forward-transform and distortion
rows (it is named as unmeasured headroom, not as a quantified gain).
